# Registry and auth only. pnpm 12 does NOT read its own settings from here.
#
# This file used to carry `engine-strict=true` and `update-notifier=false`, and
# both were inert: pnpm 12 takes every behavioural setting from
# `pnpm-workspace.yaml` and nothing else. Verified rather than assumed — the
# same `node-linker=hoisted` applies from the workspace file and changes
# nothing from here.
#
# What still works here is npm-compatible registry configuration (`registry=`,
# `//registry.npmjs.org/:_authToken=`), which pnpm reads the npm way. That is
# why the file is kept empty rather than deleted: this is where someone looks
# for that, and where they would otherwise re-add a pnpm setting that does
# nothing.
#
# Node and pnpm versions are enforced by `devEngines` in package.json. `engines`
# alone stopped being enough at pnpm 12 — see the note there.
